Subject: scsi-generic: do not start a zero-length data phase after sense

Local QEMU 10.2.3 integration-test workaround, not an upstream release fix.
mhVTL filemarks return CHECK CONDITION with a full residual and fixed sense
byte 2 = 80h. scsi_parse_sense_buf retains that FILEMARK bit in sense.key.
The sense branch bypasses the existing zero-length completion check and
calls scsi_req_data(req, 0), leaving DC-390 waiting indefinitely. Preserve
partial data on sense, but let empty results reach normal status completion.

--- a/hw/scsi/scsi-generic.c
+++ b/hw/scsi/scsi-generic.c
@@ -307,3 +307,3 @@
-        if (sense.key) {
+        if (sense.key && len > 0) {
             goto req_complete;
         }
